# build.log

## Purpose
Chronological log of routine updates -- files created or modified, and what changed. Lightweight,
one entry per change, no deep narrative. This is the "what happened, when" record.

For WHY something was hard and HOW it was solved -- major LP/modeling problems, architectural
decisions, real bugs with real consequences -- see Internal_Debugging_Log.md instead.
For recurring error patterns worth flagging so they aren't repeated -- see Common_Mistake_Log.md.
For granular, lower-level source detail behind any assumption -- see Data_Sourcing_Log.md.

Log structure established 2026-08-27, per direct user instruction, splitting what had previously
all lived in Internal_Debugging_Log.md into four purpose-specific logs. Not backfilled with every
prior-session update -- starts fresh from this point forward. Entries before this date remain in
Internal_Debugging_Log.md's own existing 125 entries, un-migrated (see that file's own updated
header for the open question on whether to retroactively re-sort them).

---

