  configuration." Investigated the actual mechanism rather than defend the number -- confirmed 820 of
  3,285 days (~25%, concentrated in winter months) hit exactly zero or near-zero. Checked the firming
  module's own solve_max_flat_level_for_window/compute_chained_daily_firm_levels directly: confirmed no
  minimum-reserve-SoC floor exists anywhere in that logic -- SoC can be driven to exactly 0.0 if that's
  what maximizes a single day's own isolated flat-level optimization, with nothing preventing it. This is
  the "midnight blindness" failure mode the uploaded generic explainer document itself named directly
  (a single-day algorithm "will routinely empty the battery in the evening"). Real, confirmed modeling
  gap, not a defensible finding as originally presented -- a fix (adding a minimum-reserve-SoC floor
  parameter) is proposed to the user directly rather than silently picked.

## 2026-09-05 (1-day lookahead result accepted as final)

- Tested the proposed reserve-floor fix directly (20%) -- found it does NOT genuinely solve the
  zero-output finding: zero-day count only dropped marginally (820 -> 808 of 3,285 days), since a
  per-day-isolated optimizer has no incentive to preserve margin beyond whatever floor exists and simply
  drains to the new floor instead of to zero, recreating the same failure mode. Reported this honestly
  rather than present a partial fix as resolved. Reserve-floor code (minimum_reserve_soc_pct, added to
  _can_hold_flat_level_without_shortfall/solve_max_flat_level_for_window/compute_chained_daily_firm_
  levels/find_optimal_blended_split, tested and confirmed working correctly in isolation) kept in the
  codebase as a real, valid, backward-compatible extension -- not the fix for this specific finding, but
  potentially useful for other analyses later.
- User accepted the 0.00 MW result as final "under these particular circumstances" -- a genuine,
  dependable, nonzero firm-capacity floor is not achievable at a 1-day, PJM-day-ahead-aligned lookahead
  for this fleet, given the real 9-year weather record. Updated Six_Day_Lookahead_Firming_Documentation.md
  with the full finding: the result itself, the investigation showing it's structural (not a bug or an
  unfixed parameter), and the practical implication for the transmission-reduction question (this fleet
  cannot support any dependable day-ahead-market firm commitment; the 3-day/6-day lookahead results remain
  the project's meaningful positive findings, since only multi-day foresight lets the algorithm prepare
  for an approaching low-solar stretch before it arrives).

Files: Six_Day_Lookahead_Firming_Documentation.md (updated, new section 5).

