## 2026-09-05 (population-based C&I/parking extrapolation, 28 additional jurisdictions)

- Built population_extrapolation.py as a proper OO structure (SES Rule 1, mirroring the same
  locality-keyed design already established in school_rooftop_solar_assumptions.py) rather than a
  one-off calculation, given the user's own request implies this is reusable, ongoing extrapolation
  logic, not a single-use script.
- Reference basis: Fairfax/Arlington/Prince William (Loudoun deliberately excluded -- documented outlier,
  data-center-driven commercial boom distorts its own C&I MW/capita far outside what any other county
  would plausibly show). C&I kW/capita range: 0.113 (Fairfax) to 1.506 (Arlington), a 13.4x spread even
  excluding Loudoun. Parking kW/capita range: 0.361 (Fairfax) to 3.845 (Prince William).
- Deduplicated the user's two source population lists directly against Virginia's real jurisdictional
  structure before building the target list, rather than assume no overlap: found and excluded 6 CDPs/
  1 incorporated town already embedded inside a county elsewhere on the list (Dale City/Woodbridge ->
  Prince William; Centreville/Reston/McLean -> Fairfax; Tuckahoe -> Henrico; Leesburg -> Loudoun) --
  would have double-counted roughly 300,000+ people had these been treated as separate. Kept Roanoke
  (independent city, 98,807) and Roanoke County (96,927) as two distinct, correctly-separate entries
  despite the confusingly similar names.
- Final target set: 28 jurisdictions (16 counties + 12 independent cities), total population 4,250,833.
- Tested (SES Rule 2): 11 tests, all passing, cross-checking against independent arithmetic
  reconstructions and verifying the deduplication logic directly (not just that some result comes out,
  but that the specific excluded entities are actually excluded and the specific expected ones remain).
- Result is a genuinely wide range (C&I: 478.6-6,402.6 MW; parking: 1,533.2-16,343.7 MW, both ~13-14x
  spread, directly inheriting the underlying reference-rate spread) -- flagged directly to the user as a
  real limitation of this extrapolation approach's own precision, not glossed over.

